---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About Eliana | The Soul Mami" description="Eliana Reyes comes from a lineage of beekeepers, farmers, and storytellers. TEDx speaker, author of two books, facilitator of 200+ circles, and a life-liver, not a guru.">

  <!-- Beat: Positioning -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The Human</span>
        <h1>Not a guru. A <em class="soul">life-liver.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I'm Eliana Reyes, The Soul Mami. Mentor, facilitator,
          author, TEDx speaker, music maker, and a highly curious
          student of this whole being-alive thing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="photo photo--arch" src="/images/eliana-frame.jpg" alt="Eliana grinning through an empty vintage picture frame in a garden" style="max-height:480px;" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Lineage -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lineage</span>
      <h2>Beekeepers, farmers, storytellers.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        That's the line I come from, and it's not just a cute origin
        story. It's the whole operating system.
      </p>
      <p>
        From the beekeepers: a respect for cycles and organic
        intelligence. You can't rush a hive, and you can't rush a soul.
      </p>
      <p>
        From the farmers: the knowing that growth is mostly invisible.
        You tend conditions. You trust seasons. The harvest comes when
        it comes.
      </p>
      <p>
        From the storytellers: the belief that we learn through story,
        movement, relationship, reflection, and play, not through
        being lectured at. People are not machines, and I refuse to
        treat you like one.
      </p>
      <p>
        What lights me up is the moment I see a seed in another human:
        a seed of curiosity that wants to live, wants to grow. My work
        is creating spaces where that seed gets sun and water: spaces
        where people feel more connected to themselves, to each other,
        and to the work they're here to do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Credentials -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Receipts</span>
        <h2>The trail so far</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          I lead with soul, but I've also put in the reps.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>200+ circles</h3>
          <p>Cohorts, workshops, and circles facilitated over the years. Rooms where people practice being human together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Two books &amp; a TEDx talk</h3>
          <!-- TODO: book titles, links, and TEDx video URL from Eliana -->
          <p>Written words and spoken ones. The TEDx stage and the page, both in service of the same message.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Music on Spotify</h3>
          <p>Original songs, independently made. Another doorway into the work, for the days words alone don't cut it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: The Core -->
  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="wrap prose center">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Core</span>
      <h2>Self-belonging is the whole thing.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Whatever The Soul Mami does, this is underneath it: do you know
        your soul? And if you know your soul, start expressing it.
        There's stuff only you came here to express, and we need to
        see it.
      </p>
      <p>
        My dream is people living and enjoying life because they know
        who they are. Giving that self to themselves, and to the world.
        In a world that profits from your self-forgetting, remembering
        who you are is a radical act. I believe in magic, in the
        unknown, in miracles. And I believe in you being the one
        you've been waiting for.
      </p>
      <p class="lead"><em class="soul">How can we feel more alive?</em> That's the question I build everything around.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Alchemy -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
      <img class="photo" src="/images/eliana-dance.jpg" alt="Eliana dancing barefoot in a yellow dress, bathed in golden studio light" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Alchemy</span>
      <h2>Bring me any emotion.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I call myself an emotional alchemist because it's literal:
        give me any emotion and I can work with it: transform it,
        transmute it, pull the lesson out of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rage, grief, numbness, jealousy, joy that scares you: none of
        it is too much and none of it is a problem. Emotions are
        information wearing a costume. I'm very, very comfortable in
        that territory, which means when you're with me, you get to be
        too.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/work-with-me/">Work with me</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/journal/">Read my journal</a>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) var(--space-section); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
